# Polytetrafluoroethylene, phase II (13/6 helix): E. S. Clark & L. T. Muus, Z. Kristallogr. 117, 119 (1962), doi:10.1524/zkri.1962.117.2-3.119
# space group P1 (c the chain axis) (No. 1), Z = 13 CF2 per cell; oblique (probably triclinic) cell at 0 C, a' = b' = 5.59 A, c = 16.88 A, gamma = 119.3 deg, p. 121; 13/6 helix on that lattice pp. 123 and 126; no atomic coordinates in the paper
# coordinates: generated from the helix symmetry and the cited lattice (tools/make_polymer_crystals.py), not refined
# correction / model: the paper treats the lattice as the periodic arrangement of the chain axes (p. 121) and gives no space group: one chain per cell, written as P1 with alpha = beta = 90 deg (c along the chain axis)
# correction / model: no atomic coordinates in the paper: the chain is generated from the 13/6 helix and the cited lattice, not refined: 13 CF2 in 6 turns span c exactly (rise 1.2985 A, twist 166.15 deg per CF2), C-C 1.54 A, C-F 1.34 A, F-C-F 108 deg (Hasegawa, Takahashi, Chatani & Tadokoro, Polym. J. 3, 600 (1972), p. 603); this gives C-C-C 115.48 deg, carbon helix radius 0.417 A and fluorine radius 1.619 A (Bunn & Howells, Nature 174, 549 (1954): 116 deg, about 0.42 A and 1.64 +- 0.05 A); one chain on the cell axis, setting angle 25 deg (the paper gives none: the one with the longest shortest F...F between chains, 2.723 A)
# hydrogens: none (perfluorinated chain)
# written in P1 with every atom of the paper's cell; 2.3468 g/cm3, shortest contacts beyond 1-3: H...H none below 3.2 A, H...X none below 3.2 A, X...X 2.59 A
